  "goodToKnow": "Der Fahrgast is a passenger on public transport or in a taxi. Every Deutsche Bahn announcement starts with Sehr geehrte Fahrgäste or Liebe Fahrgäste. EU Fahrgastrechte (passenger rights) mean you can claim 25 percent of the fare back for a delay of over an hour and 50 percent for over two hours. On planes, Germans say Passagier or Fluggast. Literally, it's a guest on the ride. Plural: die Fahrgäste."
